usage: ENCODE DCC reproducibility QC. [-h] --peaks-pr PEAKS_PR [PEAKS_PR ...]
                                      [--peak-ppr PEAK_PPR]
                                      [--peak-type {narrowPeak,regionPeak,broadPeak,gappedPeak}]
                                      [--chrsz CHRSZ] [--prefix PREFIX]
                                      [--mem-gb MEM_GB] [--out-dir OUT_DIR]
                                      [--log-level {NOTSET,DEBUG,INFO,WARNING,CRITICAL,ERROR,CRITICAL}]
                                      [peaks [peaks ...]]

IDR peak or overlap peak only.

positional arguments:
  peaks                 List of peak files from true replicates in a sorted
                        order. For example of 4 true replicates, 0,1 0,2 0,3
                        1,2 1,3 2,3. x,y means peak file from rep-x vs rep-y.

optional arguments:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --peaks-pr PEAKS_PR [PEAKS_PR ...]
                        List of peak files from pseudo replicates.
  --peak-ppr PEAK_PPR   Peak file from pooled pseudo replicate.
  --peak-type {narrowPeak,regionPeak,broadPeak,gappedPeak}
                        Peak file type.
  --chrsz CHRSZ         2-col chromosome sizes file.
  --prefix PREFIX       Basename prefix for reproducibility QC file.
  --mem-gb MEM_GB       Max. memory for this job in GB. This will be used to
                        determine GNU sort -S (defaulting to 0.5 of this
                        value). It should be total memory for this task (not
                        memory per thread).
  --out-dir OUT_DIR     Output directory.
  --log-level {NOTSET,DEBUG,INFO,WARNING,CRITICAL,ERROR,CRITICAL}
                        Log level
